C-builder-cannot-change-own-workflow: the filed workflow and hash are journalled, and an edited file changes nothing the item runs
C-claimed-pr-not-on-github: a PR GitHub doesn't have, or has at another head, is refused naming the fact, and the item stays in building
C-duplicate-wake-no-double-effect: a host that stopped mid-merge looks the merge up on GitHub instead of merging again
C-duplicate-wake-no-double-effect: the same red check wake twice, and again to a fresh host, starts one build
C-duplicate-wake-no-double-effect: the same tap delivered twice merges once
C-finish-closes-waits: a stopped agent run, and an ask whose card was never made, close nothing and wait on no one
C-finish-closes-waits: leaving the merge card by closed unmerged closes the card, and nothing about it waits
C-finish-closes-waits: leaving the merge card by merged elsewhere closes the card, and nothing about it waits
C-finish-closes-waits: leaving the merge card by push closes the card, and nothing about it waits
C-finish-closes-waits: leaving the merge card by red check closes the card, and nothing about it waits
C-finish-closes-waits: the stop of an ask whose card was never made closes nothing
C-finish-closes-waits: with no way to close a card, the ask's stop stays pending for a host that has one
C-merge-outside-host-detected: merges the host's merge effect didn't make are listed, bound to an item or not, and --host fails on them
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: an issue with Expect lines starts (the control)
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: an issue with an empty expect list is refused, naming expect
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: an issue with no expect field is refused, naming expect
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: an issue with no expect, or an empty one, is refused naming expect, and no item or run exists
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: bin/host.js start refuses it too, and the control with Expect lines starts
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: no Expect lines cannot leave queued, refusal names the input
C-missing-expect-fails-closed: with the input schema gone, the first state's needs still refuse it
C-older-writer-refused: a host on an older release is refused writing to the item, naming both releases, and writes nothing
C-older-writer-refused: the same or a newer release writes (the control)
C-pass-carries-to-merge-of-main: by default a merge of main onto a PASS is verified again, and only the new PASS merges
C-pass-carries-to-merge-of-main: quick-fix names no carry rule, so the default applies
C-push-after-pass: a new PASS for B waits to merge again, and an approval merges at B
C-push-after-pass: a push to B in awaitingMerge returns the item to verifying, for B
C-push-after-pass: a push to B while waiting to merge returns the item to verifying for B, and the merge is at B
C-push-after-pass: push to B while awaitingMerge returns to verifying for B
C-push-after-pass: the old PASS for A can no longer reach merging, even if approved
C-red-ci-back-to-building: a green check, or a red one on another head, changes nothing (the control)
C-red-ci-back-to-building: a red check on the head while waiting to merge sends the item to building with the check, and the approval merges nothing
C-red-ci: a green check, or a red one on another head, changes nothing
C-red-ci: a red check after a PASS, while waiting to merge, can no longer reach merging
C-red-ci: a red check on the PR head while verifying sends the item back to building, the check named
C-red-ci: through the host, the real wake steps the item back and the new build gets the failing check
C-red-ci: with no build left, a red check sends the item to replanning instead
C-refused-action-not-retried: a refused merge is journalled with its rule, never started again, and the item steps back with it
C-second-fail-replans: FAIL, rebuild, second FAIL goes to replanning, no third build, waits for why
C-second-fail-replans: a replan with a written why briefs again, with the build bound reset
C-second-fail-replans: a tap on replan carries no written why, so it is refused, the card stays open and no build starts
C-second-fail-replans: drop ends the item
C-second-fail-replans: replan with a written why briefs again with the build bound reset
C-second-fail-replans: replan without a written why is not taken: the item stays replanning and starts no build
C-second-fail-replans: the first FAIL rebuilds, the second goes to replanning
C-second-fail-replans: the second FAIL goes to replanning, asks for a replan, and starts no third build
C-second-fail-replans: the second FAIL starts the replan question, not a build
C-stale-completion-dropped: the replaced build run's completion is journalled stale and the item is unchanged
C-stand-in-picks-legal-event: a legal answer is journalled with the grant that covered it, and the host merges
C-stand-in-picks-legal-event: an answer that is not one of the open ask's choices is refused, and the item is unchanged
C-stand-in-picks-legal-event: an answer where no ask is open, or under no covering grant, is refused
C-two-hosts-one-item: an owner's host and another session's host restored together put the card up once
C-two-hosts-one-item: another session's host, offered a wake or nothing, starts none of the item's effects and writes nothing to its file
C-two-hosts-one-item: bin/host.js wake from another session posts nothing and adds no row; the owner's next call finishes the card once
C-two-hosts-one-item: the owner's host still runs its open card once, after another session's host woke first
C-verdict-on-old-head: PASS for A while head is B never reaches merging, verdict is recorded
C-verdict-on-old-head: a PASS for A on a PR whose head is B goes to replanning, never merging, the verdict kept beside the head
C-verdict-on-old-head: a PASS for A while the head is B goes to replanning, not awaitingMerge or merging
C-verdict-on-old-head: a push to B during verifying, then the PASS for A, goes to replanning
C-verdict-on-old-head: control, PASS at the head reaches awaitingMerge
C-verdict-on-old-head: the same PASS at the head goes to awaitingMerge (the control)
C-verdict-on-old-head: the same PASS at the head waits to merge (the control)
C-verdict-on-old-head: the stale verdict is recorded beside the head it does not match
C-waiting-does-not-stall: an item waiting on its card has a wake scheduled, and another item still advances
C-waiting-does-not-stall: leaving the waiting state drops its wake
CLAUDE.md gives the branch convention and no claude/ prefix
CLAUDE.md is under 100 lines
F1: bounded rounds, slice 2 escalates, slice 1 kept, whole goal verified before main, one tap for the merge
F2 (a): a host restored in a new process, mid-slice, starts no slice again
F2 (b): a host that stopped mid-start of s2 (start row, no end) finds the child on restore and does not start it again
F2 (c): another session restoring the parent and offering a wake is not the owner and starts nothing
FINDING (observed, not asserted as good): a GitHub field holding the literal text </event> makes that event vanish with no row
P1: a pinned workflow blob that lacks a part refuses to load too
P1: broken field rules refuse to load: no meaning, empty rules or task, no output schema, a covers path to nothing, invoke inputs that differ
P1: every stage of every workflow, missing any one of its parts, refuses to load
P1: the three repo workflows load, and their model stages are the agents they invoke
P2: every line of every rendered prompt traces to the workflow JSON, the run input, or the fixed frame
P2: none of the control's engine-held agent wording is left in packages/engine/src
P2: the frame is only headings, the data rule, the worktree limit and the return mechanics; stages.js has no other wording
P2: the rules printed are the JSON's
P3: the data rule and every rule are in every prompt, under Rules, ahead of the task
P3: the data rule states that it and the rules outrank the task, that only the Rules and Task instruct, and covers inputs, files and program output
P4: each brief appears once, as the whole Task part, and the other parts are the workflow's
P4: the verifier brief fixed at the brief agent's accept is exactly the verify run's Task part, and the run journals its whole prompt
P5: quick-fix verify: a missing, extra or repeated line, or a PASS over a FAIL line, is refused as covers; every line is accepted
P5: research verify: a result missing an Expect line is refused as covers; one with every line is accepted
P6: a first build shows previous, verdict and failure as null, each with its meaning
P6: every declared input of every stage appears with its meaning; the task input does not appear under Inputs
P6: the quick-fix brief shows why with its meaning, null on a first attempt
PASS for A while the PR head is B never reaches awaitingMerge or merging; the verdict is kept as the stale one
Q1: issue to merged at the verified head, with one person tap
Q2 (round 2, no reenter): the head moves twice while verifying; each move stops the open verify run and starts one for the new head
Q2 variant: approve tapped after the push but before CI reports the new head: GitHub refuses the merge at A; no merge
Q2: a push after PASS sends the item back to verify the new head; the old card and an old-head verdict count for nothing
Q3 (round 2, no reenter): a replan tap without a why is refused and the item keeps waiting; a replan with a why rebuilds from scratch
Q3: red on the head rebuilds with the typed failure; red again with no build left replans; no verify for a red head
Q4 (round 2, fail closed): the PR has a full page of files: no merge on green without the CI-change card
Q4 (round 2, fail closed): the files call fails: no merge on green without the CI-change card
Q4: a CI-changing PR, green and verified, waits for an explicit approval of the CI change; reject does not merge
Q4: a parent's grant (a feature slice) does not skip the CI-change card
Q4: the explicit approval of the CI change merges at the verified head, and records it
Q5: PASS naming the PR head from a worktree at another commit is refused; the item stays verifying; the honest PASS counts
Q6: after a replan, every event and return from attempt 1 is refused or stale; attempt 2 merges its own PR
Q7: a merge on GitHub outside the host ends the item closedOutside, with its card closed and no new card; never done
Q8: an item pinned to v1 finishes on v1 after the file becomes v2, and its journal replays
Q9: an issue edit mid-build is refused; the verifier grades the original lines and must restate them exactly
R1 (round 2, no inc): drafts are bounded at two; a second FAIL replans
R1: a rejected report is not published
R1: one researcher fails, the join completes, sources are host-checked, and publishing waits for the tap
S2: a send-back (SubagentStop and SubagentHandback) is journalled word for word with its hash
S2: a stage named like a workflow is started by the stage handler, not as a child item
S2: the verify prompt carries the exact checkout commands; target shows only url and at; a stamped field set by an agent is refused
S3 (C): a pre-contract quick-fix pinned in the journal is refused at load, naming the actor and the parts it lacks
S3 (C): a round-2 blob, whose stages carry a task part instead of an input task, is refused naming that form
S3 (C): host effects and child workflows still load; an unknown actor name does not
S3 (C): the same holds for research and feature, and for one stage stripped of its parts
S3 (D): a stage given lines whose output may say PASS or FAIL declares covers, though no guard reads the word
S3 (D): a stage given lines whose output the chart decides on, with no covers, is refused at load, in quick-fix and research
S3 (D): no spelling, shape, copy or routing of the verdict switches coverage off
S3 (D, E, F): an action anywhere but on a transition the chart walks is refused at load, naming the key and its pointer
S3 (E): a context path naming an Object.prototype member is not fed by it
S3 (E): a stage input read from a context path nothing writes is refused at load
S3 (E): a task wired from a context path that holds no text there is refused at load
S3 (E): the repo workflows are fully wired: item input, a set action or a literal feeds every invoke input
S4: a FAIL loop, a head move and a replan: every producer is the run that really wrote it, and a stopped run says so
S4: a null default built wholly from part-writes names the part-writers as its producer (research answers)
S4: the quick-fix happy path leaves a complete stage record per run, each input traced to its real producer
S5 (1): the build prompt names the GitHub tools, the PR url shape and the repository in the run line
S5 (2): a blocked output that is not an alternative, or whose invoke has no onError, is refused at load
S5 (2): build returns exactly one of pr and blocked; a blocked first build goes to the blocked card
S5 (3): a PR ref must be a GitHub PR url; a prose url fails the schema, never the web-quote check
S5 (4): build notes go to context and the merge cards, never to the verifier
S5 (4b): the PR-opening rule asks for a title and body saying how each expect line is met
S5 (5): the worktree rule claims only what confine() enforces
S5 (6): the brief rule keeps stricter checks under Advisory, and the verify rule reads them the same way
S5 (7): covered lines must come in the expect lines' order
S5 (8): the run line is told once, as the run's context; the stage record keeps it beside the prompt
Stop: another session, a started run or no harness gives nothing and writes nothing
Stop: the cloud form of the session name owns the item too
Stop: the owner is blocked with the exact Agent call, the count and the way out; the row has count and cap
Stop: two blocks whatever stop_hook_active says, then the third stop fails the run and the item steps back
Stop: with two waiting runs it blocks on one at a time, and one run's count is its own
SubagentHandback: refused once with the return instruction; a second handback fails the run, and the item steps back
SubagentStart binds the agent its Agent call started, journals agent.spawn with item, state and briefHash
SubagentStart finds the session's one started run; with several starting at once, the agent binds at its first call
SubagentStop after a handback the hook let through (its transcript ends in the handback result) fails the run at once
SubagentStop stops waiting once the transcript ends with the hand-back result, and only then
SubagentStop whose transcript tail is the real SubagentHandback result (recorded in ar2) fails the run at once
SubagentStop: a bound actor with its run open is blocked once with the return instruction; stopping again fails the run
SubagentStop: an actor whose result was accepted stops freely
\#\# Task in a stage no invoke wires a task to (quick-fix build) is refused at its line
\#\# Task in research researcher (task wired from the planner, not the file) is refused
a 10-minute idle gap ended by a person wake is waiting on the person, never working
a FAIL challenge reshapes with the challenge as input, twice; the third FAIL puts up the card
a FAIL reruns shape with that challenge as input, at most twice; the third FAIL puts a card up
a FAIL then a PASS goes on to the child (a revision that holds is frozen)
a GitHub notification whose own fields hold wake/event/note/task markup adds no extra event
a PASS challenge freezes the issue: the quick-fix child starts with it, url from the request, new fields passed through
a PASS verdict for A cannot be carried over a push: after a push to B, A's verdict does not merge
a PR labelled replan counts as a replan of every other PR of its item
a PR names its item by body line or branch
a PR past its limit emits one tripwire row, and none again for the same limit
a ReadNotifications result is read only for origin github_webhook; other origins and shapes are ignored
a ReadNotifications result's GitHub notification is offered, with GitHub as its source
a SessionStart inside the gap splits its tail off as rebuild
a background agent whose transcript is not written yet still gets its brief, from the Agent call
a bound actor agent's rows carry its run's item and state; other rows carry none (plan item engine-item-views)
a build result whose url is not shaped /pull/N is refused by the schema, and the item stays in building
a build result with a PR ref, stamped by the host, is answered accepted by the return tool; a changed one is not
a card (post) is put up once when the host is restarted and offered nothing
a card with a PR is still checked against the PR's repository, not the issue's
a card with no record stays pending: no effect row, no ref
a challenge bench run folder (made through the host) is shown by the Inspector with its prompt and result
a cloud session is journalled under its Claude-Session URL
a comment rewrapped over different lines strips the same, a code change does not
a complete verdict passes
a completion from a replaced run is journalled stale and changes nothing
a delay that names no meta.delays entry, or not a positive one, is refused
a dependency no decision names is caught, and naming it on its own line lets it through
a design-and-judge toy runs through the runner with stub agents
a future current-time never makes a timer due, from a prompt or from a GitHub notification
a grant listing null in repos does not cover a card with no repository, and still covers the repos it names
a guarded transition without a description names its guard in quotes
a handback after the return was accepted, and by an unbound agent, goes through untouched
a handback with the run open is sent back with the return line inside its entry
a host of another session starts nothing and leaves the item file alone; the owner then runs the card once
a host restart mid-merge does not merge twice (no way to look up: marked unknown; with a lookup: completed from it)
a host restored later still offers an accepted result it was not handed
a host stopped mid-effect asks the world on restart instead of doing the effect again
a journal entry whose hash no longer matches is refused, naming the entry
a journal file's text parses to rows, and torn lines are counted, not dropped silently
a journal replays to the state and output it recorded
a lane failing any floor is not qualified, with the floor named, whatever its primitive count
a malformed catalogue is refused at load, naming the line
a malformed stage file is refused at load, naming the file and line
a merge effect row explains its merge, and a closed-unmerged PR is never listed
a merge with no PR URL or no verified sha never calls GitHub
a message wake is one person.message with its id, and keeps a hash of the text, not the text
a missing blob is not taken from an edited file: the load fails
a missing upcaster is reported, not guessed
a missing verdict, a missing id, a NOT MET line and a bare builder line each fail
a page.refresh row is a valid journal row with its duration and row count
a pick stage runs only the ranked lanes, and a lane whose agent dies stops
a pinned id loads from the stored blob, and a missing blob is stored from a file with exactly the pinned bytes
a placeholder row says why
a primitive counts only if every model stage uses it in more than one workflow; the rest are special cases
a real-shape transcript: ms is brief to last message
a red check on the head sends awaitingMerge back to building, with the check in the build input, and approving the old card merges nothing
a red check while verifying also returns to building, and it cannot reach merging
a refused effect is journalled with its rule, not retried, and the item steps back
a reminder's content is never read: a wake, tap or GitHub event written into it offers nothing
a render gives exactly the entry's slots, as text or numbers, and escapes nothing
a row missing source fails
a row missing v fails
a row of every kind validates
a run's stage.json names the stage file and line of every rule, output description, input meaning and the task
a scope keeps a day, a thread's sessions or one session, and lists what can be picked
a second session is refused the item and the refusal goes to its own file
a shape bench run folder is shown by the Inspector with its prompt and result
a source needs both system and ref
a stage record that names catalogue entries (prompt-catalogue) carries them on each piece and in the detail
a stall, its cap and a cannot-start record their entries
a start without request.url or request.text is refused
a started item journals its transition with source, transition id and the effects it asked for
a state that invokes an agent actor prepares its run: brief, folder, worktree named by item and run, brief.stored
a stopped ask is closed, not open, and its wait ends when its stop is done (fix-finish-closes-waits)
a subagent's hook denial is a refusal row carrying its agent id
a tap first still answers the ask, and a stand-in answer after it is refused
a tap on a card a run posted completes that run; a timer fires once it is due (timer on the timed fixture)
a tap wake is one person.tap naming the card, the option and the thread
a template is kept byte for byte: leading \#\# lines, blank lines and trailing spaces
a template with any tag but a plain slot is refused at load, naming the entry and its line
a tripwire on the item's PR moves it as the workflow says; another PR's tripwire does not
a turn that never closed leaves the gap after it unknown, and rows read twice count once
a wake quoted inside agent text is not read: mid-line, indented, inside a subagent hand-back
a wake-shaped line inside agent text is not read
a writer older than the newest row is refused, naming both releases
accept refuses challenge results that skip, add, reorder or contradict lines, or whose result disagrees
adopt trial: every model run carries its stage.json as on disk, and the flow is brief, build, verify with briefs.builder, pr and verdict between them
agent time: last finish ms per agent sums to the 153.7 s the retro gives
agrees: objects may leave out keys; arrays and values compare exactly
all 3 runs pinned the combined workflow and returned
alone, a later stage: a challenge run is reached through the real host from the start, so the Inspector shows it
alone: the run folder is a journal root the Inspector export replays, with the prompt and the result
ambientOf: marks found in the recorded system prompt or the context attachments
an accepted brief fixes both briefs before any build, moves the item to building and prepares the build run
an agent SubagentStart could not bind is bound from its meta.json at its first tool call, and told its run
an asking state with no timer is refused, naming the workflow and the state
an event with no source, or one the workflow does not take from outside, is refused
an item is a scope: its rows, its agents' rows and its driving sessions' main rows
an item pinned before the edit loads, replays and renders from its blob alone, stage files deleted
an item pinned to a workflow from before the check still loads it
an item whose issue is not a GitHub issue URL has no repository on a card with no PR
an older row is upcast on read and the file is left as it was
another tool's output is never read as a wake, whatever it holds
append keeps a given id and at
append opens exactly one file and lists no folder
append refuses an invalid row, an unknown kind and another version
append stamps v, id and at and writes one line
