bin/host.js answer on the blocked card: retry builds again, replan needs --why, drop ends it; refusals change nothing
bin/host.js answer: a refused answer exits 2 and changes nothing; a granted one is journalled with its grant and the host merges at the verdict sha
bin/host.js: a card the item left waits as a pending stop until the thread withdraws it and runs `closed`
bin/host.js: a tap before the card is recorded matches nothing; after `card`, the tap merges at the verdict sha
blind reads committed with their keys, and both packets regenerate from the sets
blobs: brief and answer are blobs whose sha256 match the rows, recomputed from the transcripts
blobs: the brief and the answer are blobs whose hashes match the rows
block: a Stop from T (not the owner) gives no output and no row
block: after the run's Agent call (spawn.json) the Stop gives no output and no row
block: the cloud form (CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID set, run.session the URL) blocks too
block: the owner S is blocked with item, state, run, actor, ccp-run, Block 1 of 2 and the exit; one stall row
blocked-card-answered: drop ends the item dropped
blocked-card-answered: replan with --why moves to briefing with that why
blocked-card-answered: retry under a grant moves to building with the same briefs and the block as failure
blocked-retry: a blocked first build goes to blocked, whose card offers retry, replan and drop with the block
blocked-retry: a retried build blocked again, or a rebuild blocked, goes to replanning with replan and drop only
blocked-retry: only a block reaches the card: a stop without a return and a brief error replan as before
blocked-retry: replan from the blocked card needs a why and briefs again; drop ends; nothing else is taken
blocked-retry: retry builds again with the same briefs, the block as failure, no why and no brief run
blocked-retry: the retried build counts as the second: its PR verifies and merges, and a FAIL after it replans
blocked-route: build returns blocked naming the refused push, item at replanning, card carries "build blocked: <reason>"
both journals replay on the quick-fix they pinned (restore re-runs every transition and checks its hash)
bound outside merge: a pr.merge row naming an item explains it as journalled, but it is still listed as not made by the host
branch-stamped: own repo stamps head.ref (any case), a fork or a gone fork does not; the agent may not set it, and sees it in previous
brief: bench --prompt-only for every case equals my render() of the task literal plus the case input
brief: bench --prompt-only on the recorded input equals my render(), current workflow
brief: bench --prompt-only on the trial's pinned blob equals my render() and the committed brief.md
build writes index.html and data.js from a config, and skips missing sources by name
build: bench --prompt-only on the recorded input equals my render(), current workflow
build: bench --prompt-only on the trial's pinned blob equals my render() and the committed brief.md
builder briefs carry no PASS or FAIL condition
builder briefs quoting every expect line: runs 1 and 2 do, run 3 restates them (the accepted builder-criteria trade)
builder-criteria accepts escaped double quotes and refuses a paraphrase
builder-criteria on the verifier's own planted brief verifier-methods-copied
builder-criteria on the verifier's own planted brief verifier-paraphrased
builder: beyond Expect: an agent whose tools name the return tool completes the loop
builder: harness-works: the swap hands the agent its brief byte for byte, and SubagentStart binds it
builder: holds: only Read and Glob are called, every turn is haiku, and the marker comes from the agent body
builder: listed: the plugin loads from the skills dir and the Agent tool starts ccp-harness:probe-reader
cannot-start: a run failed at the cap is refused already-failed and keeps its stalled why
cannot-start: a started run is refused
cannot-start: an unknown run and a started run are refused and change nothing
cannot-start: from another session it is refused wrong-session and changes nothing
cannot-start: the owner fails the run with its reason; others and bad prompts change nothing
